# UI Color Tokens

Use [`src/styles/mit-theme.css`](../../src/styles/mit-theme.css) as the only source of CSS color values and `tokens.colors` from [`src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts`](../../src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) for rare inline SVG/chart styles.

- Prefer semantic utilities: `text-foreground`, `text-mit-text`, `text-mit-readable-ink`, `border-border`, `bg-card`, `Button variant="mit"`.
- Do not paste raw MIT hex values or Tailwind `blue-*` classes into auth/admin UI.
- Text links that need MIT red should usually be `text-mit-red dark:text-mit-red-ink`; avoid bare `text-mit-red` on dark-capable surfaces.
- Auth primary actions use shared shadcn controls and `Button variant="mit"`; auth inline links use `authInlineLinkClassName`.
- Keep foreground/background pairs readable in light and dark mode; use existing tokens instead of adding ad hoc accessibility rules here.
